And now, the story...

This wizard had a rather humble beginning; his notable possessions
were a scroll of enchant armor, a spellbook of magic missile, a magic
marker (0:76), and a wand of cancellation (which he never used). He
had a close call on the first level when a falling rock dropped him to
one hitpoint, but he pressed onwards. While healing in the next room,
his cat got hit by another falling rock and died. From then on (until
near the end), he went solo...

By the time I got to the Oracle, I was level 5 and starting to use
magic missile.  On the third level of Sokoban I ran across 3
shriekers, the third of which granted me poison resistance. The 4th
level yielded an amulet of reflection, as well as a wand of polymorph
from a confused-looking blue jelly.

On DLVL4 I foudn the stairs to the mines, and I descended. Shortly
after entering, I hit expert in dagger. My inventory was nearly full
most of the time, so I had to leave numerous things behind. In
Minetown, I encountered the ghost of kefka810 (who didn't have much on
him, unfortunately). While magic missiling the ghost, it accidentally
bounced and angered a shopkeeper which I was fortunately able to
appease with some spare gold. Izchak had no magic lamps for sale and
there were few other stores, so I continued to the Crypt at the bottom
(with one prayer-averted close call on the way), where I found a gray
stone (and a few spellbooks to read) and returned to the dungeon. (I
later found out that it was flint and had to run all the way back to
get the REAL luckstone).

I established my stockpile on the first level of Sokoban, dumping most
of my spellbooks and rings. On DLVL 8 I ran across a throne room
containing the ghost of elche the healer, giving me a spellbook of
extra healing. Going up a level, I managed to level from 11 to 16
thanks to a friendly succubus. A nearby leprechaun hall gave me enough
gold to donate once for protection (got 4 points). DLVL 9 yielded my
first unattended altar, which I converted and sacrificed until I got
Magicbane (rather easy, since I could case create monster). This
became my main base of operations (until later, when I moved it back
to Sokoban). DLVL 11 gave me a non-coaligned temple (much more
convenient than hiking to Minetown), and DLVL 12 gave me both a
general store (with a magic lamp) and the portal to the Quest.

The quest was fairly uneventful, throwing tengus, vampire bats, and
xorns at me. At the Locate level, I managed to jump into a pool of
water after gaining (controlled) teleportitis, and I lost a few
scrolls and a spellbook. When I met The Dark One, he immediately
picked up the Eye, rendering him immune to my now-powerful magic
missiles. By now, I was level 18 with AC -3. I teleported to the
stairs, thwacked him with Magicbane, and claimed my prize (as well as
a magic marker). I returned to the main dungeon and went to my stash,
where I sacrificed and sacrificed a bunch (creating 2 umber hulks in
the process, which ended up destroying the entire left half of the
level), gaining some intrinsic protection and a few spellbooks in the
process. It was around this time that I finally got myself a unicorn
horn.

Further down, I ran across another throne room which allowed me to
identify some of my items, revealing my aforementioned "luckstone" to
be flint. The Eye transported me right to the bottom of the mines
where I collected the *real* luckstone. At this point, I decided to
move my primary base to Sokoban 1. I continued downward. At DLVL 19, I
learned how to Jump, and did so repeatedly until I was basic at Escape
spells. Shortly afterwards, I met my first Angel, which I barely
dispatched using Drain Life. On DLVL 21, I repeated the above process
using Knock to get to basic at Matter spells. Returning to Sokoban, I
did it again with Light to get to basic at Divination spells so I
could cast Magic Mapping with less than 100% failure.

When I got to Medusa's Island, I had no easy way to cross the water.
Luckily, there was a winter wolf on one of the islands, so I used its
breath to freeze the moat. Medusa looked at my shiny armor, and I
busted open Perseus to get a sack, my first 'light' container in the
entire game. The next level down was the Castle, where a Master Lich
and an Arch-Lich teleported out to greet me (magic missile killed them
fast). I found I had no musical instrument with which to lower the
drawbridge (I had learned the passtune during a sacrifice session), so
I started creating monsters and killing them, hoping to create a
soldier with a bugle. I teleported to the mines to look for an
instrument, but managed to overlook the one that was there (a horn of
some sort). I returned to the castle and continued summoning monsters.
Eventually I got a fire giant with a boulder, so I gave up, pushed the
boulder into the moat in front of the drawbridge, and used my trusty
Force Bolt to blast the drawbridge open. I quickly cleared out the
castle and got the Wand of Wishing, with 3 charges on it.

I returned to Sokoban and wished for 2 scrolls of charging (already
had 2 markers, didn't want to risk mis-writing), +2 SDSM, and a bag of
holding (the only one I ever saw in the entire game!). Recharging the
wand, I asked for +2 boots of speed and put the wand away for the rest
of the game. This improved my AC to -22.  I returned to my altar on
DLVL9, where I repeatedly casted spells (fainting several times) to
get my skills to the point that I could advance them all upon leveling
up (drinking 2 potions of gain level to speed up the process). I then
sacrificed until I was crowned, receiving my spellbook of Finger of
Death. Lots more sacrificing was done in order to get a few more
spellbooks. I returned to Sokoban to make some holy water.

Now that I had a bag of holding, I scoured the dungeons and mines
(lighting all of the dark levels) for the items I had left behind
during my first visit. I took this opportunity to buy some candles
from Izchak. Starting at DLVL1, I mapped every level to find their
vaults. At DLVL9 I did some more sacrificing, trying (and failing) to
get another artifact. After a while, I continued down to DLVL11's
temple, where I donated my vault money and found another vault which,
for some odd reason, wouldn't let me teleport the first time. I
quickly found out that the spot I had chosen (and which was rejected)
was the portal to Fort Ludios...

I quickly cleared out the outside area and collected a large pile of
K-rations. I returned to my stash to retrieve a cursed scroll of
earth, then warped to Ludios and killed Croesus with 4 magic missiles.
Leaving the Fort, I donated my remaining money to try and get more
protection, but I got nothing but appreciation for my selfless
generousity. Stopping at Sokoban to grab my pile of rings, I found a
sink and proceeded to identify Slow Digestion and Levitation. With the
intention to do some polypiling, I warped to the Quest to collect
items I had missed or left behind. A few sacrifices later and I
decided I would go to Hell.

About halfway through clearing the Valley, I started having trouble
remembering how to cast Magic Missile. This was at around 39K turns,
so I returned to Sokoban to do some studying. A few spellbooks later,
I resumed my task of clearing and lighting the Valley. Somewhere, I
ran across a T-shirt ("Madame Elvira's House O' Succubi Employee of
the Month"). Just outside Moloch's temple, I found a spellbook which
didn't want to tell me its secrets. A quick dip in some holy water
revealed it to be Identify, a spell I had been wanting for quite some
time. I took one step into Gehennom and opened a portal back to
Sokoban. I then proceeded to identify all of my items. Examining my
magic markers, I proceeded to write a pile of enchant armor scrolls,
reducing my AC to -39. Using a few spare charges from my now-recharged
markers, I took the opportunity to genocide 'L', 'h', and ';'. Some
spare potions allowed me to level up to 27, maximizing all of my spell
skills. I then returned to Gehennom and began my descent.

Being able to cast Magic Mapping made things go a bit faster than
usual, though I didn't have any source of digging at the time (was too
lazy to find a pick-axe, and didn't feel like using up my wands).
Juiblex died to a pair of magic missiles before he ever got a chance
to touch me, after which I lit up his entire swamp. Asmodeus proved to
be troublesome, repeatedly digging his way away. In Beelzebub's lair,
I danced on some magic traps until I managed to boost my charisma from
9 to 13. I followed Asmodeus until he got to the top level of the
Wizard's tower (undiggable) where I finally killed him. Going
upstairs, I met Orcus and quickly dispatched him. I danced with a
succubus in a graveyard to gain some more hitpoints, then danced on a
magic trap to boost my charisma to 16. At this point, I realized that
my cloak of magic resistance was not fireproof (though it was somehow
resisting the numerous fire traps), so I wrote a scroll and
fireproofed it.

I continued my descent to the bottom of Gehennom, where I located the
Vibrating Square and marked it with an amulet of strangulation.
Returning to my stash, I identified my loot, refreshed my spells, and
proceeded to do a bit of polypiling. Out of the 9 amulets I had, none
turned into life saving. I returned to Gehennom to find Vlad's tower
and found it in Orcus's Ghost Town. While trying to light up a room, I
found I had forgotten (remedied by a quick visit to my stash).

I got my amulet of life saving and the Candelabrum of Invocation, as
well as a spellbook of Detect Treasure. Returning to the stash, I
dropped off some junk and did some more polypiling, giving me Cone of
Cold and Detect Unseen. I stashed my ever-growing collection of gems
in a sack and scoured the dungeon again, now having the ability to
detect objects for more polypiling goodness. On the way, I grabbed a
pick-axe and then proceeded to dig nice wide paths through Gehennom
between the stairs and collect every bit of treasure I could find.

Several thousand turns later, burdened from the loot I had collected,
I returned once more to Sokoban to refresh my spells and do one final
round of polypiling, which yielded 3 amulets of life saving, numerous
gems, and a few more spells (including Charm Monster, which proved to
be very useful later). For laughs, I enchanted my pick-axe to +5 and
rustproofed it. A bit more sacrificing and praying got me a spellbook
of Protection. I gated to Vlad's tower to begin my ascension run, only
to notice that my spells were once again running low. I warped back to
Sokoban, refreshed my spells once more (around 60K turns by now), did
some sacrificing and praying (got Teleport Away), donated my excess
gold, and decided to begin my ascension run.

I made my way through the Wizard's tower, clearing it easily. When I
made it to Rodney's chamber, I suddenly realized that I had forgotten
the other invocation artifacts! I warped to Sokoban, grabbed the bell
and candelabrum, and resumed my task. I dug a hole into Rodney's
chamber and gave him the finger before he even came out to greet me.
On my way to the vibrating square, Rodney visited me, getting the
finger immediately.

Upon reaching the Vibrating Square, I performed the invocation and
descended into the Sanctum. Rodney promptly greeted me and quickly
dropped dead. For some reason, all of the priests in the sanctum were
sleeping in a small cluster below the temple, making it rather easy to
dispatch them. Stepping into the temple, I gave the high priest the
finger, collected the Amulet (naming it THE REAL THING), and began my
ascent.

Rodney visited me twice on the way up, and I felt The Force a total of
8 times. Once I was clear of Gehennom, I ran as fast as I could to
DLVL1, stopping at Sokoban to refresh my spells one last time, dump
out my remaining loot, and enchant Magicbane to +7 (at this point, the
damage was far more important than the special effects). Using my last
magic marker, I wrote a blessed scroll of genocide ("just in case" I
needed it on the Planes) and a 4th scroll of gold detection (I had
found 3).

Upon reaching Earth, I gave Rodney the finger for the last time and
learned the spell of Dig. Recharging my energy (and levitating, I
stepped into the plane of Air. The air elementals were somewhat
troublesome, though they only took 4 magic missiles to kill. Some
steam vortices provided adequare shelter for restoring my energy. As I
neared the portal, I tried out my nice Charm Monster spell and gained
a few pets (which got left behind) and I warped to Fire. Near the
portal, an Archon showed up and caused numerous problems, as I
couldn't stay blind and non-stunned. Charm Monster helped reduce the
crowds around me, and I managed to step onto Water without further
incident. I sat around in the original bubble for a while until it
merged with a large one, which turned out to contain the portal to the
Astral Plane.

I started by going to the left, where I met Pestilence, another
Archon, and Anhur's temple. Turning around, I suddenly got surrounded
by monsters, including a few dragons, so I quickly read my blessed
scroll of genocide. To my horror, I found out I was confused as I read
the scroll, then breathed a heavy sigh of relief after realizing that
confused self-genocide only happens with non-blessed scrolls. I
continued to the center temple, guarded by Famine, which turned out to
be Ptah's. My heart racing, I made my way to the altar on the right,
smacking Death with a few magic missiles each time he got too close,
then stepped on Thoth's high altar. Having 2 charges left on my wand
of wishing, I wished for 4 dilithium crystals (only got 3) and tried
to wrest the last charge out of the wand. Eventually I gave up, and
sacrificed the amulet.

